2026-10-28T17:23:13.8180065Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFJXgnUjn8dtMR6NTmN2QU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 12,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/12\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"Support SES S/MIME signing with ACM certificates (`AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate` / `MessageSecurityOptions`)\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### What new functionality are you requesting?\\n\\n* `aws_sesv2_email_identity_certificate` (new resource, or new attribute block on `aws_sesv2_email_identity`)\\n* `aws_sesv2_configuration_set` (enhancement \\u2014 new `message_security_options` argument)\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nAmazon SES now supports S/MIME signing of outbound email using X.509 certificates managed in AWS Certificate Manager (ACM). This has two parts, both currently unsupported by the provider:\\n\\n1. Associating an ACM certificate with an email identity's From address, via the `AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate` / `DisassociateEmailIdentityCertificate` / `ListEmailIdentityCertificates` SES v2 API operations (equivalent to `aws sesv2 associate-email-identity-certificate`). There is currently no Terraform resource to manage this association.\\n2. Enabling S/MIME signing on a configuration set via `UpdateConfigurationSet` with a `MessageSecurityOptions` object (equivalent to `aws sesv2 update-configuration-set --message-security-options '{\\\"SigningScheme\\\":{\\\"Smime\\\":{}}}'`). `aws_sesv2_configuration_set` has no `message_security_options` argument today.\\n\\nWithout these, S/MIME/ACM signing for SES can only be configured out-of-band via the AWS CLI/API, outside of Terraform-managed state.\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_sesv2_email_identity_certificate\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  email_identity  = aws_sesv2_email_identity.example.email_identity\\n  from_address    = \\\"sender@example.com\\\"\\n  certificate_arn = aws_acm_certificate.smime.arn\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_sesv2_configuration_set\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  configuration_set_name = \\\"example\\\"\\n\\n  message_security_options {\\n    signing_scheme = \\\"SMIME\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### References\\n\\n* AWS SDK for Go v2: [`AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate`](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/sesv2#Client.AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate) (added in SDK v1.71.0)\\n* AWS docs: [Authenticating email with S/MIME in Amazon SES](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-authentication-smime.html)\\n* AWS docs: [Attaching a certificate to an email identity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-authentication-smime-associate.html)\\n* AWS docs: [Enabling S/MIME signing on a configuration set](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-authentication-smime-enable.html)\\n* AWS CLI: [`associate-email-identity-certificate`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/sesv2/associate-email-identity-certificate.html), [`update-configuration-set`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/sesv2/update-configuration-set.html)\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [],\n10\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:12Z\",\n11\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-07T14:59:50Z\"\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bbcd3aa-f8d6-47fc-8479-646105e31148","uuid":"ef4fb51e-939f-446a-80a3-6af8378bfd19","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:23:13.808Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 12,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/12\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"Support SES S/MIME signing with ACM certificates (`AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate` / `MessageSecurityOptions`)\",\n  \"body\": \"### What new functionality are you requesting?\\n\\n* `aws_sesv2_email_identity_certificate` (new resource, or new attribute block on `aws_sesv2_email_identity`)\\n* `aws_sesv2_configuration_set` (enhancement \\u2014 new `message_security_options` argument)\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nAmazon SES now supports S/MIME signing of outbound email using X.509 certificates managed in AWS Certificate Manager (ACM). This has two parts, both currently unsupported by the provider:\\n\\n1. Associating an ACM certificate with an email identity's From address, via the `AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate` / `DisassociateEmailIdentityCertificate` / `ListEmailIdentityCertificates` SES v2 API operations (equivalent to `aws sesv2 associate-email-identity-certificate`). There is currently no Terraform resource to manage this association.\\n2. Enabling S/MIME signing on a configuration set via `UpdateConfigurationSet` with a `MessageSecurityOptions` object (equivalent to `aws sesv2 update-configuration-set --message-security-options '{\\\"SigningScheme\\\":{\\\"Smime\\\":{}}}'`). `aws_sesv2_configuration_set` has no `message_security_options` argument today.\\n\\nWithout these, S/MIME/ACM signing for SES can only be configured out-of-band via the AWS CLI/API, outside of Terraform-managed state.\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_sesv2_email_identity_certificate\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  email_identity  = aws_sesv2_email_identity.example.email_identity\\n  from_address    = \\\"sender@example.com\\\"\\n  certificate_arn = aws_acm_certificate.smime.arn\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_sesv2_configuration_set\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  configuration_set_name = \\\"example\\\"\\n\\n  message_security_options {\\n    signing_scheme = \\\"SMIME\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### References\\n\\n* AWS SDK for Go v2: [`AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate`](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/sesv2#Client.AssociateEmailIdentityCertificate) (added in SDK v1.71.0)\\n* AWS docs: [Authenticating email with S/MIME in Amazon SES](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-authentication-smime.html)\\n* AWS docs: [Attaching a certificate to an email identity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-authentication-smime-associate.html)\\n* AWS docs: [Enabling S/MIME signing on a configuration set](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-email-authentication-smime-enable.html)\\n* AWS CLI: [`associate-email-identity-certificate`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/sesv2/associate-email-identity-certificate.html), [`update-configuration-set`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/sesv2/update-configuration-set.html)\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:12Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-07T14:59:50Z\"\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NFJXgnUjn8dtMR6NTmN2QU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
