xportable public certificates\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"> AWS Certificate Manager introduces public certificates you can use anywhere * [Announcement]( * [Blog post]( Requires AWS SDK for Go v2 [Release 2025-06-17]( * aws_acm_certificate\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-06-18T19:18:16Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.203,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 48727,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#48727\",\n      \"title\": \"ACME support in AWS Certificate Manager\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"> Today we\\u2019re announcing ACME support for public certificates in [AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)]( * [Announcement]( * [Blog post]( Requires AWS SDK for Go v2 [Release 2026-06-30](\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-07-01T16:13:19Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.177,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46671,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46671\",\n      \"title\": \"Support for SES `Email feedback forwarding` configuration for Domain Identity\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"aws_sesv2_domain_identity_feedback_attributes similar to Do the same but for Domain Identity It re-opens only introduces setting management for Email Identity but NOT for Domain Identity \\\\- * * No\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T15:30:50Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.174,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 22924,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#22924\",\n      \"title\": \"ses email identity recreated after being verified\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"I have created ses email identity through TF then verified it successfully. When I applied the same script for other changes, The email identity is created again and pending verification. resource \\\"aws_ses_email_identity\\\" \\\"ses_email\\\" { count 